# HTTP Status Codes Guide

| Code | Meaning | QA Usage | Developer Note |
|------|---------|----------|----------------|
| 200 | OK | Expected for successful GET | Default success response |
| 201 | Created | Use for POST requests | New resource created |
| 400 | Bad Request | Invalid input test cases | Client-side error |
| 401 | Unauthorized | Auth failure tests | Missing/invalid token |
| 404 | Not Found | Resource not found tests | Invalid resource ID |
| 500 | Server Error | System error tests | Server-side failure |

Tips:
- QA: Include these in `expected_status_code`
- Developers: Handle all status codes appropriately

